# =============================================================================
# CRYPTODEX FRONTEND - Vercel (or Railway) environment variables.  TEMPLATE.
# =============================================================================
#
# Next.js inlines every NEXT_PUBLIC_* value into the JavaScript bundle AT BUILD
# TIME.  Two consequences, and both have bitten this project:
#
#   1. Setting a variable after the build changes nothing.  You must REDEPLOY
#      (Vercel: "Redeploy" with "use existing build cache" OFF) for a change to
#      reach the browser.
#   2. Every value here ships to the client.  Nothing genuinely secret may go in
#      this file.  Neither of the two keys below is secret - one is a public JWT
#      audience key, the other is a shared constant that already ships inside the
#      backend source - but do not add anything that is.
#
# Set these in Vercel: Project -> Settings -> Environment Variables, scope
# "Production" (and "Preview" if you use preview deploys).
#
# WHY EVERY API URL IS THE SAME HOST.  All three backends sit behind one gateway
# on one Railway service (deploy/gateway.mjs), routed by path prefix.  The
# frontend therefore points every API base at the same origin.  Do not add a path
# suffix to any of them - in particular NEXT_PUBLIC_SOCKET_URL, which socket.io
# reads as a NAMESPACE and not as a path.  See deploy/routes.mjs.
# =============================================================================


# --- The API origin.  All five are the same value. ---------------------------
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=https://<your-api-service>.up.railway.app
NEXT_PUBLIC_USER_API=https://<your-api-service>.up.railway.app
NEXT_PUBLIC_WALLET_API=https://<your-api-service>.up.railway.app
NEXT_PUBLIC_SPOT_API=https://<your-api-service>.up.railway.app
NEXT_PUBLIC_SOCKET_URL=https://<your-api-service>.up.railway.app

# --- This site's own origin --------------------------------------------------
# No trailing slash.  Must match FRONT_URL on the API service.
NEXT_PUBLIC_FRONT_URL=https://<your-frontend>.vercel.app


# --- The two keys that must AGREE with the backend ---------------------------

# NEXT_PUBLIC_SECRET_KEY IS GONE, DELIBERATELY. DO NOT ADD IT BACK.
#
# It used to be set to the API's SECRET_KEY -- the key that signs every session
# JWT. Every NEXT_PUBLIC_* value is inlined into the JavaScript bundle at build
# time and served to every visitor, so that made the signing key public: anyone
# who opened the site could mint a valid token for any account.
#
# Nothing in the frontend ever read it. It holds an opaque token and verifies
# nothing; the backends do the verifying. SECRET_KEY belongs on the API service
# and nowhere else.

# REQUIRED.  Must equal the backends' `cryptoSecretKey`, which is a CONSTANT in
# each service's config/index.js and is NOT settable from the environment.  The
# browser AES-encrypts every order body with this value and spotapi decrypts with
# that constant, so a mismatch makes every single order fail with
#   {"errors":{"token":"INVALID"}}
# and nothing else - no server error, no log line naming the key.  This has
# already broken this venue once.
#
# DO NOT INVENT A VALUE AND DO NOT COPY ONE FROM ANOTHER DEPLOYMENT.  Copy it
# from cryptodex-frontend/.env.local.example, which carries
# the correct 64-character hex constant, and verify it against `cryptoSecretKey`
# in cryptodex-spotapi/config/index.js.
NEXT_PUBLIC_CRYPTO_SECRET_KEY=<copy from .env.local.example - do not invent>


# --- Behaviour ---------------------------------------------------------------

# Anything other than the literal string "local" enables the 30-minute idle
# logout in pages/_app.tsx.  In production that is what you want.
NEXT_PUBLIC_MODE=production


# --- Leave blank -------------------------------------------------------------

# The register form does not enforce reCAPTCHA on this venue, and _app.tsx only
# mounts GoogleReCaptchaProvider when a key is present, so blank is safe and
# correct.  Setting a site key here WITHOUT a matching secret on the backend
# would mount the provider against a server that never verifies it.
NEXT_PUBLIC_RECAPTCHA_KEY=

# DEAD - the admin panel was removed and NOTHING READS THIS ANY MORE: there is
# no ADMIN_URL key in config/index.js.  Setting it has no effect; delete it.
NEXT_PUBLIC_ADMIN_URL=

# DEAD - read into config as `getGeoInfo` and `ONRAMP_APP_ID`; no component
# consumes either.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_GEO_INFO=
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ONRAMP_APP_ID=


# =============================================================================
# THE OTHER FRONTEND ENV FILE, AND WHY IT DOES NOTHING
# =============================================================================
# cryptodex-frontend/local.env spells every key with a
# DOUBLE underscore (NEXT_PUBLIC__USER_API) while config/index.js reads a SINGLE
# one.  Nothing in local.env has ever reached the application; it exists only
# because `npm run dev` is `env-cmd -f local.env next dev` and env-cmd refuses to
# start without the file.  Do not copy local.env into Vercel - it would set
# nothing while looking as though it had set everything.
